CAT = "iepsaLaw"; SEG = "LAW"
# Private Security Services Act 2004 (revised, Law Reform Commission, read 5 Nov 2026): ss. 2, 6, 8,
# 21, 22, 23, 26, 27, 27A, 29, 30, 32, 33, 36, 37, 38, 39, 40, 41; Private Security (Licensing and
# Qualifications) Regulations 2022 (S.I. 574/2022) as amended by S.I. 204/2024; Private Security
# (Identity Badge) Regulations 2024 (S.I. 588/2024); Private Security (Licensing and Standards)
# Regulations 2023 (S.I. 140/2023).
Q = [
("Which body licenses security guards in Ireland?",
 "The Private Security Authority", ["An Garda Síochána", "Quality and Qualifications Ireland", "The Health and Safety Authority"],
 "Section 6 of the Private Security Services Act 2004 established the Private Security Authority (PSA), and section 8 gives it the job of granting and renewing licences. QQI makes the training award; it does not license anyone."),
("Under the Private Security Services Act 2004, what is the PSA's main function?",
 "Control and supervise providers", ["Prosecute every security offence", "Train all new security staff", "Set guards' rates of pay"],
 "Section 8(1) says the Authority shall control and supervise persons providing security services and maintain and improve standards in those services."),
("Which QQI award is the training qualification for a security guard (guarding) licence?",
 "4N20604 Security Guarding Skills", ["4N20611 Door Security Skills", "4N22384 Enforcement Guard Skills", "5N1356 Occupational First Aid"],
 "The Private Security (Licensing and Qualifications) Regulations 2022, as amended in 2024, set QQI Level 4 minor award 4N20604 Security Guarding Skills, or an equivalent, for this licence. 4N20611 is the door supervisor award."),
("A bouncer controls entry to a nightclub for pay. Which licence category covers this work?",
 "Door supervisor", ["Security guard (guarding)", "Enforcement guard", "Private investigator"],
 "The Act defines a door supervisor as a person who, for remuneration, controls entry to premises or a place where an event is held, monitors behaviour there, or removes people because of their behaviour."),
("Under the Act, the PSA must refuse a licence to an individual who is:",
 "Under 18", ["Under 21", "Not an Irish citizen", "Living outside Dublin"],
 "Section 22(3)(a) obliges the Authority to refuse an individual who is not a fit and proper person, is under 18, does not comply with the Act or regulations, or has not paid the prescribed fee."),
("Which personal test does section 22 apply when the PSA decides on a licence?",
 "Being a fit and proper person", ["Having two years' experience", "Holding a full driving licence", "Passing a fitness test"],
 "The Authority must refuse a licence if it is satisfied the applicant is not a fit and proper person to provide a security service. Experience and driving licences are not requirements of section 22."),
("A guard's employer asks to transfer his licence to a new recruit. What does the Act say?",
 "It cannot be transferred", ["It may be transferred once", "Only with PSA approval first", "Only within the same company"],
 "Section 22(5) says a licence does not confer any right of property and may not be transferred, assigned, mortgaged or charged."),
("You applied to renew your licence on time but the PSA has not decided before it expires. What happens?",
 "The licence stays in force", ["You must stop work that day", "You get a 7-day permit", "You must reapply from scratch"],
 "Section 23(3) says that if a renewal application is not determined before the licence expires, the licence continues in force until the application is decided."),
("What must a licensed guard carry while providing the security service?",
 "The PSA identity card", ["A copy of the 2004 Act", "A letter from the Gardaí", "The QQI certificate"],
 "Section 29(2)(a) says each individual licensee shall have the identity card in his or her possession when providing the security service authorised by the licence."),
("A client at a site asks a guard on duty to show his PSA identity card. What must he do?",
 "Produce it then and there", ["Refuse unless a Garda asks", "Show it at the end of shift", "Send a copy by email"],
 "Section 29(2)(b) requires the licensee to produce the card there and then, on request, to any person for whom the security service is being provided, and to let that person inspect it."),
("Apart from a Garda, who else can require a guard to produce the PSA identity card?",
 "A PSA inspector", ["Any member of the public", "A local councillor", "The site's cleaning staff"],
 "Section 29(3) lets a member of the Garda Síochána require production of the card, and section 29(6) gives the same power to an inspector of the Authority."),
("How does a uniformed security guard (guarding) licence holder show his licence number to the public?",
 "Wearing the PSA badge", ["Saying it when asked", "Writing it on the jacket", "A notice at reception"],
 "Section 30 and the Private Security (Identity Badge) Regulations 2024 require security guard (guarding) licence holders to wear the badge, which is the PSA identity card, clearly visible when worn."),
("When may a security guard (guarding) licence holder work without wearing the identity badge?",
 "During covert work", ["When it is raining", "When working overnight", "When the site is closed"],
 "The 2024 Identity Badge Regulations exempt a guarding licence holder while it is necessary for the service that members of the public should not be aware the person is providing it, such as covert work."),
("A guard leaves the security industry for good. What must she do with her licence and identity card?",
 "Surrender them to the PSA", ["Keep them in case she returns", "Give them to her employer", "Destroy them at home"],
 "Section 32(1) says that when a licence is suspended, revoked or expires, or the licensee ceases to provide a security service, the licence and identity card must be surrendered to the Authority."),
("A licensed guard is charged with an offence and the case is pending. What does section 36 require?",
 "Notify the PSA", ["Wait for the verdict first", "Tell only the employer", "Nothing until convicted"],
 "Section 36(1) requires an applicant or licensee convicted of an offence, or against whom proceedings are pending, to notify the Authority in the prescribed manner and period."),
("A company hires a man with no PSA licence to guard a warehouse. Who commits an offence under section 38?",
 "The company hiring him", ["Only the unlicensed man", "Only the warehouse owner", "Nobody, if he is trained"],
 "Section 38 makes it an offence to employ or engage a person to provide a security service if that person must hold a licence and does not. The unlicensed man also commits an offence under section 37."),
("What is a defence for an employer accused of hiring an unlicensed guard?",
 "The guard showed a PSA card", ["The guard was on probation", "The job lasted one night", "The guard was paid in cash"],
 "Section 38(3) makes it a defence to prove that the person providing the service produced his or her identity card or licence to the defendant."),
("Who can find out whether a particular guard holds a PSA licence?",
 "Anyone, via the register", ["Only the Gardaí", "Only licensed employers", "Only the guard's own family"],
 "Section 33 requires the PSA to keep the Private Security Register and make it available free of charge to the public, including on its website."),
("A shopper believes a guard acted improperly. Under section 39, how may she complain to the PSA?",
 "In writing", ["Only through a solicitor", "Only by phone", "Only through the Gardaí"],
 "Section 39(1) says any person may make a complaint in writing to the Authority about a licensee's conduct in providing a security service."),
("After investigating a complaint, which of these can the PSA impose on a licensee?",
 "A reprimand", ["A prison sentence", "A wage deduction", "A driving ban"],
 "Section 39(3) lets the Authority revoke or suspend the licence, or give a reprimand, warning, caution or advice. Imprisonment is for a court."),
("The PSA proposes to revoke a licence. How long does the licensee have to make written representations?",
 "14 days", ["7 days", "28 days", "3 months"],
 "Section 27(1) requires the Authority to notify the licensee of its proposal and consider written representations made within 14 days. Where safety is at risk, section 26(2) lets it act without this step."),
("Which independent body hears appeals against PSA licensing decisions?",
 "The Private Security Appeal Board", ["The Workplace Relations Commission", "The District Court only", "The Policing Authority"],
 "Section 40 established the Private Security Appeal Board, independent in performing its functions, to hear and determine appeals against decisions of the Authority."),
("Under section 27A, who may the PSA give a temporary licence of up to 6 months?",
 "A new applicant", ["A guard whose licence is suspended", "A guard renewing a licence", "Any guard on a short contract"],
 "Section 27A allows a temporary licence of up to 6 months so an applicant who meets the other requirements can show the necessary competence. It does not apply to renewals."),
("A man hands out cards calling himself a licensed security guard, but holds no licence. What does this break?",
 "Section 37 of the 2004 Act", ["The Equal Status Act", "The Data Protection Act", "Section 4 of the Theft Act"],
 "Section 37(1) forbids a person to hold himself or herself out, by advertisement, by displaying a shield or card or otherwise, as available to provide a security service without a licence."),
]
